  "current_review_test_status": "Supplied tests statically inspected only; independently authored controls, if any, are separately identified.",
  "mathematical_scope": "Importance-sampled time-domain sparse surrogate with all-bin unitary DFT additive l2 or l1-ceiling error; head-tail variants and Parseval support lower bound.",
  "cost_scope": "O(N) scans plus samples and input-pruned full output, claimed O(N log(k+2)); default head candidate planning O(N log log N). Fixed epsilon error is coarse versus natural per-bin scale; no exact FFT claim.",
  "test_and_evidence_limitations": "Hoeffding/union theorem is mathematical ideal arithmetic; floating norm overflow, CDF rounding and user samples can break guarantees. Supplied samples bypass epsilon/delta validation, zero inputs return before parameter guards. AccuracyTradeoff reports theoretical inner width even k>N without dense fallback clamp.",
  "findings": "Material stale-plan defect: sparsify_head_tail accepts external HeadTailPlan checking only n, then scales fresh residual samples by old plan.tail_l1 and uses old budget/method. Reusing a same-length plan on scaled input biases surrogate and invalidates guarantee. For head0/sample-tail plan from all-ones n1024 reused on all-twos, estimator DC stays1024 before unitary normalization instead of2048, independently of sampled indices. Head-only plans from a small tail can also silently discard a new large tail. Plan freshness/epsilon/delta must be revalidated.",
  "source_line_evidence": [
    "9-20 additive guarantee and standard importance-sampling attribution",
    "111-150 sample budget and scale",
    "175-208 bypass/dense fallback ordering",
    "253-270 theoretical count proxy",
    "324-386 data-dependent head-tail plan",
    "399-421 length-only plan check and stale tail_l1 scaling",
    "451-487 Parseval/natural-scale limitation"
  ],
